wolf3dgeneric @PROJECT_VERSION@ - Windows release
=====================================

This folder contains:

  wolf3dgeneric.exe       Win32 video, input, timing, and audio host
  wolf3dgeneric.dll       Platform-neutral wolf3dgeneric engine
  Nuked-OPL3.dll          Replaceable LGPL-2.1-or-later OPL emulator
  COPYING.txt             wolf3dgeneric license
  COPYING.Nuked-OPL3.txt  Nuked-OPL3 license
  THIRD_PARTY.md          Third-party provenance and revision

Game data is not included. Copy the files from an original supported game into
this folder beside wolf3dgeneric.exe, then run the executable. Supported data
extensions are WL1, WL6, SOD, SDM, SD1, SD2, and SD3.

The original SIGNON and PC-13 screens appear automatically. SIGNON artwork is
embedded in the engine as it was in the DOS executable: WL1 selects Apogee,
WL6 selects GT, and Spear selects its own screen. Use --signon apogee, gt, id,
activision, or spear to override that choice. Its memory and hardware markers
are filled at runtime using the original screen coordinates and color ramps.

If this folder contains more than one game, open a terminal here and select the
desired extension explicitly:

  wolf3dgeneric.exe --game WL6
  wolf3dgeneric.exe --game SOD

Renaming the executable to a name beginning with "wolf" prefers WL1/WL6 data.
A name beginning with "spear" or "sod" prefers SOD/SDM/SD1/SD2/SD3 data. You
may instead keep game files elsewhere and pass --data "C:\path\to\game".

wolf3dgeneric.dll and Nuked-OPL3.dll must remain beside the executable. The
Win32 executable is only a platform host and loads the engine from the first
DLL. Nuked-OPL3.dll may be replaced with a compatible modified build, as
provided for by its GNU Lesser General Public License. Corresponding source is
identified in THIRD_PARTY.md and is included in the wolf3dgeneric source
distribution.

Configuration and saved games use the process working directory and retain the
selected game's data extension.
